From 727d8b492b0af160f5b5622eef447118c96596ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:29:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] Add agent.carry_forward_instruction flag

The manual carry-forward sentence ("Include any context you want to carry
forward in your reply, along with the action you want to take.") was tied
to provides_continuous_conversation in _build_system_prompt, so it could
not be ablated in manual_rolling. analysis_mode also re-added it.

- New optional boolean agent.carry_forward_instruction (default true).
  When false, the manual_rolling / previous_response_id system prompt
  omits the sentence, including the analysis_mode prompt. With the flag
  off, the normal prompt equals the continuous-conversation prompt.
- Defaults are byte-identical to the previous prompts.
- Config validation requires a boolean and rejects `true` with
  continuous_conversation, which always omits the sentence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
